# Crossroads Oak
# Source: King's Quest VI (VGA) - reference/kq6/r03-c02.png; reframed with:
#   pnpm grid reference/kq6/r03-c02.png --name kq6-r03-c02
# Method: translated by eye. Kept: the great forked oak and its canopy, the branches reaching
#   right, the pile of grey boulders, the dirt path forking round the tree, the white castle on
#   its green hill with the winding path, the village at far left, the small rock in the lower
#   left, and the bank of ferns in the lower right. Dropped: sun rays, the hazy peaks behind
#   the castle, individual leaves and grass blades, the stone steps' detail, flowers in the
#   grass, most of the fern texture. Moved: the village sits a little higher to clear the path.
# Colours: pale hazy sky → lightblue, castle → white / lightgrey, hill and lit
#   grass → lightgreen, tall grass → green with lightgreen blades, bark → brown with black
#   grooves and yellow highlights, boulders → lightgrey / darkgrey, path → brown with yellow
#   ruts, village → yellow, dark teal ferns → cyan, ferns → green, olive frond → lightgreen.
scene "Crossroads Oak"
variants day

# ---- sky and castle --------------------------------------------------------------------
# (delay: the viewer paints these backdrops last, farthest last, filling in behind the rest; the
# picture itself is unchanged)
delay 3 {
  color lightblue
  rect 0, 0, 159, 70
}

fn tower(x, top, w) {
  shape([[x, 38], [x, top], [x + w, top], [x + w, 38]], white, darkgrey)
  shape([[x - 1, top], [x + w / 2, top - 7], [x + w + 1, top]], lightgrey, darkgrey)
  color darkgrey
  line x + w / 2, top + 3, x + w / 2, top + 4
}
shape([[118, 39], [118, 30], [158, 30], [158, 39]], white, darkgrey)
shape([[118, 39], [118, 30], [125, 30], [125, 39]], lightgrey, darkgrey)
